       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because of the dose. The FDA-labeled maximum for amlodipine in adults is **10 mg once daily**, and 20 mg is double that. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little extra blood pressure control.\n\nYou could do one of the following:\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily and add a second agent**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic, if 10 mg isn't enough.\n3. **Enter 20 mg PO once daily as written.** I'll do this if you confirm the dose is intentional. I'd add a note such as \"Dose exceeds labeled max; confirmed by attending.\"\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
